      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): catch unhandled rejection from handleGatewayEvent in event callback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe ACP gateway's `onEvent` callback dispatches gateway events to the translator via `void agent?.handleGatewayEvent(evt)` — a fire-and-forget async call. `handleGatewayEvent` awaits `handleChatEvent` and `handleAgentEvent`, neither of which has a top-level try-catch. If either method throws, the rejection becomes an unhandled rejection.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/acp/translator.ts`: wrap `handleGatewayEvent` body in try-catch so all dispatch errors are logged via `this.log()` instead of escaping as unhandled rejections.\n- `src/acp/translator.error-kind.test.ts`: add regression test verifying the error boundary catches dispatch failures.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Code path**: `handleGatewayEvent` (translator.ts:356)\n- **Environment tested with**: Node.js v24 — real process-level unhandledRejection tracking + vitest regression suite.\n- **Evidence**:\n\n```\n=== #100558: ACP handleGatewayEvent error boundary ===\n\nBefore — fire-and-forget WITHOUT error handling:\n  void someAsync();\n  => 1 unhandled rejection escaped to process\n\nAfter — fire-and-forget WITH try-catch:\n  try { await someAsync(); } catch { log(err); }\n  => 0 rejections (error caught and logged internally)\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\nScenario                         Unhandled Rejections\nBefore (original code)           1 rejection escaped\nAfter  (try-catch boundary)      0 rejections (caught and logged)\n```\n\nRegression test (translator.error-kind.test.ts): 4 passed (incl. \"catches and logs handleChatEvent failures\"). server.startup.test.ts: 12 passed.\n",
        "branch": "fix/acp-catch-gateway-event-rejection-clean",
